==English==
[[Image:USS Winston S. Churchill.jpg|thumb|A destroyer (warship)]]

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|destroy|er|id2=agent noun}}. Designating a warship, it is ellipsis of {{m|en|torpedo-boat destroyer}}, the longer term appearing at the end of the 19th century and the shorter form early in the 20th.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dəˈstɹɔɪ.ɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-destroyer.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪ.ə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# That which [[destroy]]s something.
# {{lb|en|military|historical}} A small, fast [[warship]] with light [[gun]] [[armament]], smaller than a [[cruiser]], but bigger than a [[frigate]].
# {{lb|en|military}} A larger [[warship]] with [[guided missile]] armament, usually intended for air defence or anti-ship roles. Often, but not always, larger than a [[frigate]] and smaller than a [[cruiser]].
## {{lb|en|science fiction|by extension}} A [[starship]] of comparable role.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|one who destroys}} {{l|en|devastator}}, {{l|en|decimator}}

